{
  "_comment": "soname to dependency token, per consumer. 'rpm' holds soname provides for fpm: every RPM distro exposes them identically, so one .rpm installs on Fedora, openSUSE, and RHEL alike (Fedora names the package gtk3, openSUSE names it libgtk-3-0, and both provide libgtk-3.so.0()(64bit)). 'apt' holds Debian package names, used both by fpm and by the tarball preflight. 'dnf', 'pacman', and 'zypper' hold human-readable package names and are used only by the tarball's install.sh, which prints a command for the user to run. An entry may instead carry 'exclude' with a reason, meaning the soname is known and deliberately not a package dependency; an entry that is absent altogether still fails the build.",
  "libgtk-3.so.0": {
    "apt": "libgtk-3-0",
    "rpm": "libgtk-3.so.0()(64bit)",
    "dnf": "gtk3",
    "pacman": "gtk3",
    "zypper": "libgtk-3-0"
  },
